{
  "texts": [
    {
      "content": "The Spinegrass grows in clusters of long, lanceolate leaves, rigid as needles, in crimson-brown tones.",
      "left": "142px",
      "top": "265px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "Its deep root system enables it to colonize arid and compact soils, functioning as a natural stabilizer against erosion.",
      "left": "73px",
      "top": "309px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "Each leaf carries microscopic serrated edges capable of tearing animal tissue on contact,\n\n",
      "left": "195px",
      "top": "354px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "making it an accidental trap for small organisms.",
      "left": "365px",
      "top": "398px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "Certain local insects lay their eggs at its base,",
      "left": "127px",
      "top": "448px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
    {
      "content": "taking advantage of the protection provided by the spines.",
      "left": "506px",
      "top": "448px",
      "scale": "1",
      "rotate": "0",
      "fontFamily": "melonfruit",
      "fontSize": "28px",
      "color": "rgb(17, 17, 17)"
    },
